\subsection{F1: All Variable-Rate Configurations Degrade}
\label{sec:f1}

Every configuration that introduces $\dt > 1$ imagination degrades relative to the $\dt{=}1$ baseline (Figure~\ref{fig:learning_curves}). The baseline reaches 915.7 at 105K; fixed $\dt{=}2$ (006) peaks at 485.3 before collapsing to 132.9 ($14\%$ of baseline); fixed $\dt{=}4$ (007) never exceeds 176.9 ($19\%$); the learned gate (005) collapses to 98.8 ($11\%$).

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.65\columnwidth]{figures/paper/fig1_learning_curves.pdf}
\caption{Learning curves. The baseline (black) reaches 915.7; all variable-rate configurations degrade.}
\label{fig:learning_curves}
\end{figure}

%% ============================================================
%% F2: Trained dt_embedding → nve > 1.5x
%% ============================================================

\subsection{F2: Trained Temporal Embedding Triggers Value Overestimation}
\label{sec:f2}

The factorial design isolates trained $\dt$-embedding as the causal trigger. Comparing exp\_008d (trained, subsample ON) against exp\_008f (no embedding, subsample ON): 008d reaches $\nve = 4.12\times$ and collapses (eval 82.8), while 008f maintains $\nve \leq 0.97\times$ (eval 503.0). The $\nve \geq 1.5\times$ threshold (35K+ window) correctly classifies 11 of 12 experimental configurations (AUROC${=}0.926$; Figure~\ref{fig:nve_trajectory}).\footnote{Excluding 3 baseline configurations, the 8-experiment subset yields accuracy$\,{=}\,$7/8 and AUROC$\,{=}\,$0.867.}

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.65\columnwidth]{figures/fig1_nve_trajectory.pdf}
\caption{NVE trajectories (mean $\pm$ seed range). Trained $\dt$-embedding (red, $n{=}3$) exceeds the $1.5\times$ threshold (dashed) in all seeds; no-embedding control (blue) remains near $1.0\times$. Three trajectory types emerge: early collapse (seed~0), late-onset collapse (seed~3), and self-correction (seed~2). Dotted line marks the 35K diagnostic window onset.}
\label{fig:nve_trajectory}
\end{figure}

The trained $\dt$-embedding triggers CIVO in all three tested seeds (peak NVE: $4.12\times$, $1.62\times$, $1.53\times$; all $\geq 1.5\times$ threshold), universally degrading performance to below 30\% of baseline (mean eval 206.2, 22.5\% of baseline). Downstream trajectories diverge: seed~1 (008d) undergoes immediate full collapse (eval 82.8, 9.0\% of baseline), seed~3 (008d\_s3) exhibits late-onset collapse still in progress at 105K (eval 268, train returns declining 70\% over final 8K steps), while seed~2 (009b) self-corrects after transient overestimation (eval 267.9, 29.3\% of baseline). This pattern establishes universal CIVO onset with stochastic downstream resolution: collapse is the majority outcome (2/3 seeds) but exhibits variable onset timing (35K vs 70K steps). The 1/3 self-correction case remains severely degraded. This confirms that CIVO universally damages performance regardless of whether full collapse follows (Appendix~\ref{sec:seed_divergence}).

